# Trustfile — Enaction Engine trust boundaries

@abstract:
Repository, secret, licence, external-provider, and runtime/tooling trust
boundaries for Enaction Engine.
@end

## Agent trust

Agents may read, edit, build, test, lint, and format within the repository.
Destructive actions, external publication, provider settings, releases, and
licence changes require the authority stated by repository policy.

## Integrity invariants

### no-secrets-committed
- description: No common credential files are committed
- run: test ! -f .env && test ! -f credentials.json && test ! -f .env.local && test ! -f .env.production
- severity: critical

### no-private-keys
- description: No private key files are committed
- run: "! find . -name '*.pem' -o -name '*.key' -o -name 'id_rsa' -o -name 'id_ed25519' 2>/dev/null | grep -v target | head -1 | grep -q ."
- severity: critical

### licence-content
- description: Code licence remains AGPL-3.0-or-later and prose remains CC-BY-SA-4.0
- run: grep -q 'GNU AFFERO GENERAL PUBLIC LICENSE' LICENSE && grep -q 'CC-BY-SA-4.0' README.adoc
- severity: critical

### provider-identity
- description: External badges are absent until canonical provider targets resolve
- run: "! grep -q 'sonarcloud.io/api/project_badges\\|api.scorecard.dev/projects' README.adoc"
- severity: warning

### ums-boundary
- description: Runtime does not depend on UMS Studio and released games consume compiled packages
- run: grep -q 'Enaction Engine must not depend on the UMS application' docs/architecture/UMS-INTEGRATION.adoc && grep -q 'Released games consume compiled assets or packages' docs/architecture/UMS-INTEGRATION.adoc
- severity: critical
